{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1’s native firewalld/nftables firewall persistently. SSH and TCP 8080 are permitted; unrelated inbound connections are rejected. The policy survived a verified node reboot. CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Removed the Cockpit/9090 and DHCPv6-client allowances.","Kept SSH enabled, allowed TCP 8080, and set the public zone target to REJECT.","Verified effective nftables rules and tested ingress through an isolated network namespace.","Restarted node1 once and verified its changed boot identity, service recovery, persistent rules, SSH listener, and firewall behavior."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent firewall permits SSH and TCP 8080 while rejecting unrelated inbound connections","command_ids":["cmd-408cc7258a454371","cmd-3167bf5648754a88"],"summary":"Runtime and permanent public-zone configuration contains only SSH and TCP 8080, with a REJECT target. Effective nftables rules accept TCP 22/8080 and reject unmatched input."},{"requirement":"Functional firewall behavior","command_ids":["cmd-4c5765297c464a40","cmd-1fd00035722e4545"],"summary":"Before and after reboot, TCP 8080 returned HTTP 200 through the public zone, while TCP 9090 was rejected even though a listener existed."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-52ac4457e41041b8","cmd-c9a8fe3885d04857","cmd-00b30005debc4bc8","cmd-034b0bbd50894efa","cmd-1fd00035722e4545"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 5b620f5a-2111-4f37-b111-4cdf414707cf was captured; the safe reboot was acknowledged; post-reboot boot ID changed to 6ad64e3b-90cb-4f32-82c0-9e4754da9d36. Firewalld and sshd recovered active/enabled, SSH was listening, and the persistent firewall policy and functional behavior recovered."}]}
